WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.980
Thank you, everyone.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.520
We know people are concerned and want
to keep their families and loved ones safe.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.120
There’s a lot of bad information
out there right now.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.680
And the CIDC just wants to issue
some basic common-sense guidelines

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.000
that everyone should follow during this crisis.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.960
#1: Wash your hands with soap for at least
20 seconds coming up to the wrists.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.360
#2: You just want to clean and disinfect
any frequently touched surfaces or objects

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.600
like countertops or doorknobs.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:31.840
#3: If you do have to cough or sneeze, do it
into a tissue and then discard that tissue.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.560
I don’t know why have to tell anybody that.
Who keeps a used Kleenex?

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.520
If you need to sneeze or cough
and don’t have a tissue, just try to

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.200
sneeze away from the people you’re with.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.440
If you’re surrounded by people...

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.640
I don’t know, just try to sneeze
toward someone you don’t like.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.480
I’m just kidding. Don’t do that.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.800
What you can do is you can sneeze
or cough into the crook of your elbow.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:56.360
So kind of like (sneeze) like that and that
will keep the germs from spreading.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.920
Don’t worry that was just a demonstration.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.000
Don’t touch your face.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.920
Don’t shake another person’s hand.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.320
Don’t shake another person’s face.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.560
In general, you want to avoid close contact.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.200
Remember that expression “I wouldn’t
touch them with a 10-foot pole?”

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.480
I know we’ve had that conversation, Jill.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.640
So just think of it not a 10-foot pole...

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.440
It’s a six-foot pole, and you
don’t want to touch anybody with it.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.440
Or if you do just make sure you
disinfect that pole when you’re done.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.160
You don‘t wanna be in any large group.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.120
So we recommend you avoid
any groups more than 500 people.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.760
So like a concert or a...

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.160
I’m sorry, any groups larger than 200 people.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:37.320
So if you see more than 50 people,
don’t go in that group.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.160
Okay 10 people. So if...

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.080
You know what?
Just don’t get any groups at all.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.160
If you see another person just
run the other way.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.200
If you do go into a public
place, like say a grocery store...

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.680
Make sure you buy at least
two years worth of toilet paper.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.440
In general, if the shelf looks empty and
there’s only one or two items left, just buy them.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.200
It doesn’t matter if you need them or not.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.720
It’s also a great time to stock up on
those foods you’re never gonna eat.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.680
Anything that’s shelf-stable that
you want to keep in your bunker.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.210
Like cans of lima beans, creamed corn,

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:08.729
Vienna sausages, canned okra, hearts of palm,
large containers of garlic salt,

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:10.680
Any of those are great options.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.400
Obviously don’t drink Corona beer.
I think we all know that.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:18.960
But even Dos Equis, those two X’s are like
the skull &amp; crossbones on a bottle of poison.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:23.360
And I’m told that Modelo is
the Spanish word for death.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.400
You want to stay away from all Chinese products.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.880
Don’t eat Chinese food.
Remember: lo mein, high risk.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.900
Don’t play Chinese checkers.
Don’t watch Chinese films.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:38.640
You know that old expression:
Chinese. Fight disease. Look at these.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.600
There was some misleading information
about the film Parasite,

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.360
the Oscar winner this past year,
that I would like to clear up.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.720
You won’t catch anything from
watching this film.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.060
In fact it’s not even Chinese, it’s Korean.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.640
So that makes it one of the
safest films you can watch.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.860
Now there’s a side effect of this
social distancing we’re all doing.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:02.140
A condition known as Cabin Fever.
(Coincidentally another Oscar-winning film.)

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.320
But this is in no way
related to the coronavirus.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.160
There are several ways you can combat this:

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.100
Any sort of social interaction you can do
with the people you’re confined with.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:15.060
Like playing games, having a fun
little 80s sing-along night.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:19.500
So like you could cheer yourself up by
singing the song ”Come on, Eileen.“

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.180
And substitute the lyrics “COVID-19.”

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:27.060
A second option suggested by our staff
is the song "Hey, Mickey.”

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.980
So it would go something like this:

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:35.360
C-O-V-D-1-9. In our homes we are
confined. Hey sicky! Hey sicky!

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:42.780
C-O-V-D-1-9. Cause the markets
to decline. Hey sicky! Hey sicky!

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.680
Just you know anything that’s fun like that.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.480
In short, as Americans, and frankly
as citizens of the world,

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.260
The best advice we can give here
at the CIDC is that we all come together.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.360
I mean, not literally.
I mean stay away from each other.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:01.520
But separately we can unite to lick this coronavirus.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.280
Again, not literally.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:06.860
Thank you. And stay safe.

